 "_comment": "Tests that need artifacts the repository deliberately does not publish (raw data, trained model files and checkpoints, feature tables, row-level prediction files; see .gitignore). Key: 'module::test'. Value: glob patterns relative to the project root; the test is runnable only if every pattern matches at least one file. The core runner (scripts/run_core_tests.py) reports a test whose pattern has no match as NOT RUN (artifact missing), never as passed, and --require-artifacts turns that into a failure. The tests themselves are unchanged and run, with their full assertions, whenever the artifacts exist. Regenerate the artifacts with the project's build and training scripts (README section 4). Six transaction-level evidence files (300 validation transactions each: TransactionIDs with model contributions, counterfactual effects or feature values) are kept local and not published since 2026-10-22, in line with the .gitignore publication policy; the tests that read them are listed here.",
